    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, carrying a massive 83.29 efficiency score. Facing a favorable matchup against Brown, he benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a premium leadoff spot, making him our highest-upside play for both power and counting stats. **Kyle Tucker** (79.07) and **Andy Pages** (73.31) follow closely as elite outfield options; both exploit a soft matchup against Yarbrough, with **Kyle Tucker** specifically maintaining high value despite the slight dynamic platoon tax. While **Nasim Nunez** (65.67) and **Curtis Mead** (60.34) occupy the middle of the order, their scores are inflated significantly by the +10% park factor against the struggling Lopez, providing a high-floor opportunity to chase RBI and runs in a hitter-friendly environment.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.83). Despite his talent, his matchup against Burke presents a suboptimal skill profile relative to our starting infield, forcing him to the bench in favor of more efficient platoon alignments. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Heliot Ramos** (42.82); his low score is largely due to a tough encounter with Gilbert, making him a candidate to be swapped if a more favorable pinch-hitter becomes available. **Drake Baldwin** (49.27) and **Liam Hicks** (43.48) remain in the lineup as our primary catchers, though their proximity to the floor means they will be on a short leash if early at-bats prove unproductive. We are also keeping a wary eye on **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut and sits below our 40-point efficiency floor due to a daunting assignment against Skenes.",
